  "name": "update-and-remove-mapping-sets",
  "description": "The other two verbs on the layer contract `7.0.0` added, in one exchange: a pair re-pointed at another implementation type, a second pair added to the same set, and an empty set removed whole. Re-pointing edits `implementation`, because `application` is the pair's identity inside the set and pairing a different application type is a different pair — the distinction the collection's `identityField` declares and the immutability rule enforces.",
  "kind": "example",
  "context": {
    "summary": "The `examples/basic` model with two application types and two mapping sets seeded. `PhysicalMapping` pairs `VehicleSpeed_Kph` with the value type `float32`; `LegacyMapping` was declared before its pairs were known and still holds none, which is legal — a set is a container. No component names either set, so removing one leaves nothing dangling.",
